NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# Configure deployed Worker secrets with:
# npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
# npx wrangler secret put FIRECRAWL_API_KEY
# npx wrangler secret put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# npx wrangler secret put SUPABASE_URL
# npx wrangler secret put CLAIM_EMBED_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# npx wrangler secret put CATALOG_SYNC_SECRET
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY
# npx wrangler secret put GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID
# npx wrangler secret put RD_SHEET_ID
# Create the audit queues once before deploying:
# npx wrangler queues create claims-portal-audits
# npx wrangler queues create claims-portal-audits-dlq
# Configure a Supabase Database Webhook for public.claims INSERT/UPDATE events
# to POST to /api/embed-claims with Authorization: Bearer <same secret>.
# Include the old row on UPDATE so changed claim_text values are re-embedded.
# Configure a Supabase Database Webhook for public.claim_submissions INSERT/UPDATE events
# to POST pending rows to /api/audit (status resets to pending will requeue audits).
# For local Wrangler development, add these values to .dev.vars instead of committing them.